  "issue_date": "2024-09-20",
  "report_week": "38",
  "report_period": "Week 38 (13th Sep to 20th Sep 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Okouchi Kaiun have committed their Ultramax \"Queen Sapphire\" 61/2011 Iwagi, Japan (SS 12/2026, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at region USD 21 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-younger \"Dolce Vita\" 61/2012 Oshima, Japan (SS 09/2027, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 23,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Tolani Group committed their \"Prabhu Mihikaa\" 55/2005 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 11,85 mill. For comparison, the two-year-younger sister vessel \"Tai Hunter\" 55/2007 Oshima, Japan (SS 12/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in June at USD 14,8 mill. The OHBS Handysize \"Elegant Emilie\" 33/2008 Shin Kochi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) of Taylor Maritime was committed at USD 12,5 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Graceful Gertrude\" 33/2008 Shin Kochi, Japan (SS 08/2028, DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at USD 12,3 mill. Moreover, same owners committed the \"Sassy Sofia\" 32/2005 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) to Lebanese interests at USD 9 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Hainan Island\" 32/2004 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at USD 8,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Great Eastern Shipping have committed their Suezmax \"Jag Lalit\" 158/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 07/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1B) to undisclosed interests at region USD 33 mill. Remind you that back in June, the \"Seoul Spirit\" 160/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 34,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 11,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 20,000/21,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 16,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China into Red Sea were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Trips from Philippines into China were fixed around usd 16,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 170K/180K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. West African trips into Continent were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. US Gulf trips were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into Continent- Mediterranean range were fixed around usd 16,000/19,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into North Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
